  sumEn="In 383 the soldiers of Britain made their general emperor of Rome. He ruled the West for five years, and Wales has never let him go. Welsh tradition made Macsen the husband of Elen of Caernarfon, the father of royal lines, the founder of Brittany, and the man with whom the story of the Welsh nation begins.",
